//RS /// D-CLI-FIELD-MARKERS1=A: one-letter alias for a `#[CLI]` field.
//RS pub const MARKER_SHORT: &str = "Short"; // D-CLI-FIELD-MARKERS1
//RS /// D-CLI-FIELD-MARKERS1=A: environment fallback for a value `#[CLI]` field.
//RS pub const MARKER_ENV: &str = "Env"; // D-CLI-FIELD-MARKERS1
//RS /// D-CALLDUAL1=E: marks the first bare-read parameter of a free function as
//RS /// the receiver for the equivalent `value.function(…)` spelling.
//RS pub const MARKER_ROOT: &str = "Root";
//RS 
//RS /// D-CABI-PLATFORM1=A: per-function native calling-convention marker for C
//RS /// declarations. C remains the implicit default; alternate ABIs never inherit.
//RS pub const MARKER_ABI: &str = "ABI"; // D-CABI-PLATFORM1
//RS 
//RS /// D-BOUND-UNDO1=A: `#Undo(inverse)` names the compensating function a
//RS /// foreign binding registers on the enclosing transaction's rollback path.
//RS pub const MARKER_UNDO: &str = "Undo"; // D-BOUND-UNDO1
//RS 
//RS /// D-FFI-CAP1=A: `#Close(close)` joins a returned foreign handle to the
//RS /// consuming `close(^handle)` protocol. The named foreign function is checked
//RS /// against the returned handle before the binding is registered.
//RS pub const MARKER_CLOSE: &str = "Close"; // D-FFI-CAP1
//RS 
//RS /// D-LINTPOLICY1=A / D-DECIMAL1: per-site lint-suppression marker —
//RS /// `#[allow(lint_name)]` on a struct or field (e.g. `#[allow(float_money)]`
//RS /// silences the default-on `float_money` lint). Deliberately lowercase: it
//RS /// names a lint, not a declaration-shaped feature, so it does not
//RS /// follow the PascalCase marker convention. Struct/field site collection:
